/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6641b4f-e396-5ff5-8410-bd9f53c4e8d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-98339" :question/problem "Which of the curves below is simple, closed, and negatively oriented?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A simple closed curve is positively oriented if, when traveling along it, one always has the curve interior to the left and the curve exterior to the right. Otherwise, the curve is negatively oriented. \n\nA curve is positively oriented if it is traversed counterclockwise and is negatively oriented if it is traversed clockwise.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the curves:\n\n- Curve I is neither simple nor closed.\n\n- Curve II is a simple and closed curve but it is not negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed counterclockwise, so it is positively oriented.\n\n- Curve III is simple, closed, negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\n- Curve IV is simple, closed, negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is curves III and IV only"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418155 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162016 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c94ec9c4-650f-5d39-9294-651b03b172bf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Singular Value Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44bf1c7c-6b0e-563e-954c-3195f51957e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454208} {:answer/id #uuid "da6a0750-c545-55b0-96a6-f69075551811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44bf1c7c-6b0e-563e-954c-3195f51957e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454208} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5818556-f363-51a8-99fb-0d3f96f4adeb" :answer-field/key "$Σ$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8908ac85-0ea3-5a1c-b891-38df1e4efa1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454210} {:answer/id #uuid "c681945d-6fe4-577f-97ef-2ee6b13ef95b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c681945d-6fe4-577f-97ef-2ee6b13ef95b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454211} :answer-field/id #uuid "27f45678-b73d-5101-b847-456979724eed" :answer-field/key "$V$ is an orthogonal $4\\times 4$ matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454855} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a3a2869-1fca-522a-9ef5-456efad708a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454212} {:answer/id #uuid "0d94671b-f829-5477-b5c4-2a0aa1a5da65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a3a2869-1fca-522a-9ef5-456efad708a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454212} :answer-field/id #uuid "0749b39f-5020-520c-b5a7-35e6e06dd907" :answer-field/key "$U$ is a diagonal matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d3ee109-94d4-53ed-8971-ac2ef97dce27" :question/math-academy-id "q-95901" :question/problem "Given the singular value decomposition $A=UΣ{V}^{T},$ where $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $m\\times n$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $m\\times m$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $n\\times n$ matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “$Σ$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix” is false. Since $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, $Σ$ must be a $3\\times 4$ matrix.\n\n- Statement “$V$ is an orthogonal $4\\times 4$ matrix” is true. Indeed, since $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix,the matrix $V$ in the singular value decomposition $UΣ{V}^{T}$ must be orthogonal $4\\times 4$ matrix.\n\n- Statement “$U$ is a diagonal matrix” is false. The matrix $U$ must be orthogonal but not necessarily diagonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$V$ is an orthogonal $4\\times 4$ matrix” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "630cd12d-1141-51ae-8f2e-a881622868e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Transitive Relations in Special Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f66032c-e554-543d-8fb7-d02dece4fb60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472988} {:answer/id #uuid "503722a1-9d9c-52aa-81fc-6a411eae1066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "503722a1-9d9c-52aa-81fc-6a411eae1066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472989} :answer-field/id #uuid "ded48b57-0e55-5867-8ce5-09520070f5ca" :answer-field/key "${R}_{1}=∅$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf4b3082-da87-5935-8a6d-c02d7c283455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472990} {:answer/id #uuid "60bece86-b150-57aa-9c00-90ecd30c70e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60bece86-b150-57aa-9c00-90ecd30c70e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472991} :answer-field/id #uuid "755bfb35-b9d2-5062-b4ab-e488a159dfa7" :answer-field/key "${R}_{2}={A}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "279c4aba-6d55-5a04-b286-e063ea4fc0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472992} {:answer/id #uuid "733b09d3-0ca0-56fd-b468-a6f12122fc9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "733b09d3-0ca0-56fd-b468-a6f12122fc9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472993} :answer-field/id #uuid "242b2c29-1e00-59da-9422-d72051cd8ab7" :answer-field/key "${R}_{3}={(5,5)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473891} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbf5caaf-107c-5cf9-9a1b-17712be4c02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472994} {:answer/id #uuid "bf886d4c-aafd-5159-a9c1-995083aabdef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf886d4c-aafd-5159-a9c1-995083aabdef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472995} :answer-field/id #uuid "18afe69d-87a8-5ebb-b3e6-8e65d1302ff0" :answer-field/key "${R}_{4}={(5,1),(7,3)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "202c6abf-dfb5-522a-9256-456835ce12bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-214430" :question/problem "Which of the following relations on the set $A={1,3,5,7}$ are transitive?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$ defined on a set $A$ is *transitive* if, for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,z)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(x,z)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if the pairs $(x,y)$ and $(y,z)$ belong to a transitive relation, then the pair $(x,z)$ should also be in the relation.\n\nIt's sufficient to check all the \"linked\" pairs of the form $(x,y)$ with $x\\ne y$ and $(y,z)$ with $y\\ne z:$\n\nMoreover, we recall the following:\n\n- The universal relation $R={A}^{2}$ is transitive since it includes all possible ordered pairs.\n\n- The empty relation $R=∅$ is vacuously transitive since the antecedent in the implication is always false, and therefore the implication is always true.\n\n- A relation containing no \"linked\" pairs is always transitive.\n\n- A relation containing only reflexive pairs is always transitive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations:\n\n- ${R}_{1}$ is transitive since it's the empty relation. $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{2}$ is transitive since it's the universal relation. $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{3}$ is transitive since it contains only reflexive pairs.  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{4}$ is transitive since it contains no \"linked\" pairs.  $\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${R}_{1}=∅$; ${R}_{2}={A}^{2}$; ${R}_{3}={(5,5)}$; ${R}_{4}={(5,1),(7,3)}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "630cd12d-1141-51ae-8f2e-a881622868e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Transitive Relations in Special Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a299c676-d4bd-5e7c-9a2c-0554e7b11068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472996} {:answer/id #uuid "94f3ebe8-49c9-50b3-a868-e5d33ab917ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94f3ebe8-49c9-50b3-a868-e5d33ab917ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472997} :answer-field/id #uuid "174d226d-d258-5803-bd1a-f8c8044e8e61" :answer-field/key "${R}_{1}={(♢,♢),(♣,♣)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e37eca59-a651-5ae5-a63a-f7c00a6e9ee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472998} {:answer/id #uuid "d58460b0-5da4-55d1-9273-6866444c5ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d58460b0-5da4-55d1-9273-6866444c5ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472999} :answer-field/id #uuid "64720d48-f6ec-5b01-9b7a-d890a7e21109" :answer-field/key "${R}_{2}={(♠,♠)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2625fa0-6fd0-5b37-8bcb-85e89aaf9f1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473000} {:answer/id #uuid "6549efa0-c3e5-513f-a9c4-a86cc73d7989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6549efa0-c3e5-513f-a9c4-a86cc73d7989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473001} :answer-field/id #uuid "1908c829-a51f-5ba0-bef7-0ed5edbdf979" :answer-field/key "${R}_{3}={(♢,♠),(♡,♣)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473895} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ead24d32-9ef3-517d-bc6c-fa5541e27250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473002} {:answer/id #uuid "9afd106d-a0c9-585d-8d8b-f5c66a4f5e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9afd106d-a0c9-585d-8d8b-f5c66a4f5e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473003} :answer-field/id #uuid "586bc858-e57d-5502-9bc1-05c0b7811913" :answer-field/key "${R}_{4}=∅$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44cd3428-3b1c-5e19-9525-5e86c3ca616a" :question/math-academy-id "q-214431" :question/problem "Which of the following relations on the set $A={♢,♡,♠,♣}$ are transitive?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$ defined on a set $A$ is *transitive* if, for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,z)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(x,z)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if the pairs $(x,y)$ and $(y,z)$ belong to a transitive relation, then the pair $(x,z)$ should also be in the relation.\n\nIt's sufficient to check all the \"linked\" pairs of the form $(x,y)$ with $x\\ne y$ and $(y,z)$ with $y\\ne z:$\n\nMoreover, we recall the following:\n\n- The universal relation $R={A}^{2}$ is transitive since it includes all possible ordered pairs.\n\n- The empty relation $R=∅$ is vacuously transitive since the antecedent in the implication is always false, and therefore the implication is always true.\n\n- A relation containing no \"linked\" pairs is always transitive.\n\n- A relation containing only reflexive pairs is always transitive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations:\n\n- ${R}_{1}$ is transitive since it contains only reflexive pairs.  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{2}$ is transitive since it contains only reflexive pairs.  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{3}$ is transitive since it contains no \"linked\" pairs.  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${R}_{4}$ is transitive since it's the empty relation. $\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${R}_{1}={(♢,♢),(♣,♣)}$; ${R}_{2}={(♠,♠)}$; ${R}_{3}={(♢,♠),(♡,♣)}$; ${R}_{4}=∅$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418246 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203887 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f65dc026-1ec7-51f3-abc2-4a8ce95f9c2c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Transitive Relations From a Digraph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4db8a7d3-abfe-5da7-8f35-9f33f9974fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472982} {:answer/id #uuid "bee0ee00-25f3-5d6b-ab69-c0475d9b0cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4db8a7d3-abfe-5da7-8f35-9f33f9974fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472982} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4178680-7a42-51f7-b05b-b18ebe268db9" :answer-field/key "![Digraph I](images/bc/bc7fc1e0c4dc7759c9dfee0d4d0d9d1a9283a94a789a76e1beb32d1b14b5a6ed.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473886} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "820a5684-a957-5349-a0f0-7963f49ebe66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472984} {:answer/id #uuid "93478089-576c-5503-80b8-3e9d093c765c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93478089-576c-5503-80b8-3e9d093c765c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472985} :answer-field/id #uuid "b558f1b5-b2d4-5cbe-8db1-9b06242983c2" :answer-field/key "![Digraph II](images/06/0633e83cd02b0f1ccbae6864ec3a4bc6d9b5938d3752feec8e2828af45b891e9.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e021bd35-f594-5b3a-b63d-34b162014252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472986} {:answer/id #uuid "e516049f-9d3f-5de6-aacd-690ed76c7a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e021bd35-f594-5b3a-b63d-34b162014252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472986} :answer-field/id #uuid "739e0d22-4e64-5fd6-9771-aa129ae1e27d" :answer-field/key "![Digraph III](images/0f/0ffc73b0defbc843db41a396bf59d1c6454e658a6ec93e84f2363dcba7ec05c7.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64ea6724-f6be-5851-a399-860e0e1924d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-214065" :question/problem "Which of the below digraphs represents a transitive relation defined on the set $A={p,q,r}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$ defined on a set $A$ is *transitive* if, for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,z)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(x,z)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if the pairs $(x,y)$ and $(y,z)$ belong to a transitive relation, then the pair $(x,z)$ should also be in the relation.\n\nIt's sufficient to check all the \"linked\" pairs of the form $(x,y)$ with $x\\ne y$ and $(y,z)$ with $y\\ne z.$\n\nIn terms of a digraph, if we have \"linked\" arrows $x\\to y$ and $y\\to z,$ then the arrow $x\\to z$ must be in the digraph too.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our digraphs.\n\n- Digraph I does not represent a transitive relation. It has arrows $q\\to r$ and $r\\to p,$ but has no arrow $q\\to p.$\n\n- Digraph II represents a transitive relation. For any pair of arrows $x\\to y$ and $y\\to z,$ the arrow  $x\\to z$ also belongs to the digraph.\n\n- Digraph III does not represent a transitive relation. It has arrows $p\\to q$ and $q\\to r,$ but has no arrow $p\\to r.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is digraph II only"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "947f058c-4c47-52df-8c28-aed016d2b148" :knowledge-point/title "Transitive Relations Defined On Infinite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4570740-e38d-5619-a596-b27434de2acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472976} {:answer/id #uuid "2445e097-f060-51a2-9b4f-786c2564057b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2445e097-f060-51a2-9b4f-786c2564057b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472977} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2928ca7-454a-561d-a28f-37c83fce06c0" :answer-field/key "$x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∣y,$ defined on $Z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a72744f6-7c6e-5b96-8a5c-21c64adc05c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472978} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8c1316-7031-5bf4-b390-e30b6262259d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a72744f6-7c6e-5b96-8a5c-21c64adc05c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472978} :answer-field/id #uuid "540b176a-d122-565a-8e22-9c2f73677d72" :answer-field/key "$x\\,S\\,y$ if and only if $x+y<4,$ defined on $R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0db7216-4608-5567-9227-6f5edb180769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472980} {:answer/id #uuid "808ff085-7391-520c-bb65-0806364a6656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "808ff085-7391-520c-bb65-0806364a6656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472981} :answer-field/id #uuid "7315c86a-eebd-57ce-ac6f-9eaaeeb953b9" :answer-field/key "$x\\,T\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4),$ defined on $Z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70eb9024-0964-59ad-a103-f6948d25a78c" :question/math-academy-id "q-214002" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are transitive?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A binary relation $R$ defined on a set $A$ is *transitive* if, for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,z)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(x,z)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if the pairs $(x,y)$ and $(y,z)$ belong to a transitive relation, then the pair $(x,z)$ should also be in the relation.\n\nIt's sufficient to check all the \"linked\" pairs of the form $(x,y)$ with $x\\ne y$ and $(y,z)$ with $y\\ne z.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is transitive. Indeed, if $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,x)\\in R,$ then $(x,z)\\in R.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx∣y\\,\\text{and}\\,y∣z\\,⟹\\,x∣z\n$$\n\nfor all $x,y,z\\in Z.$\n\n- Relation $S$ is not transitive. Notice that \n\n- $(1,-4)\\in S$ since $1+(-4)=-3<4,$ and\n\n- $(-4,5)\\in S$ since $-4+5=1<4,$ but\n\n- $(1,5)\\notin S$ since $1+5=6≮4.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is transitive. Indeed, if $(x,y)\\in T$ and $(y,x)\\in T,$ then $(x,z)\\in T.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\\,\\text{and}\\,y≡z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\\,⟹\\,x≡z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\n$$\n\nfor all $x,y,z\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$R$ and $T$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418768 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b03ea89-5152-5ff4-813a-ca985d60ed5b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7c78237-7ba8-5f5d-a33b-f0e13b1bcaf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454048} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ae988e-f035-54a7-a23f-739a60fc9826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7c78237-7ba8-5f5d-a33b-f0e13b1bcaf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454048} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3a1a93b-7a1e-598e-9ac9-1fec0a8541af" :answer-field/key "$u⊥H,\\,$ where $H={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1121815-b4cb-5a43-b5a6-e6c5f54f549f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454050} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc194be-1802-5b3c-9ead-0634aaac6f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdc194be-1802-5b3c-9ead-0634aaac6f8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454051} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c705186-a967-52c8-8f4b-6be1b77a56ab" :answer-field/key "$u⊥V,\\,$ where $V={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454775} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac97a943-76b0-577f-974e-60a75af70b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454052} {:answer/id #uuid "5c3399ef-8ee6-5f98-9847-2e8f4d1a6f50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac97a943-76b0-577f-974e-60a75af70b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454052} :answer-field/id #uuid "b18f9b5e-6144-516e-bca1-6e1944599bbe" :answer-field/key "$u⊥W,\\,$ where $W={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac83e377-f632-58f6-8bed-4004335968a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-80514" :question/problem "For the vector $u=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $H,V$ and $W$ as ${{h}_{1},{h}_{2}},{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ and ${{w}_{1},{w}_{2},{w}_{3}}$, respectively.  \n\nNow, we have to compute the dot product between $u$ and the vectors in each set. \n\n- For the set $H:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {h}_{1} & =(-2)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 0+(-4)\\cdot (-1)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {h}_{2} & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot (-2)+(-4)\\cdot 1=-8\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥̸H.$\n\n- For the set $V:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {v}_{1} & =(-2)\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 0=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {v}_{2} & =(-2)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 3+(-4)\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥V.$\n\n- For the set $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1} & =(-2)\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 3=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2} & =(-2)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 0+(-4)\\cdot (-2)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{3} & =(-2)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot (-2)=3\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥̸W.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$u⊥V,\\,$ where $V={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}\\end{bmatrix}}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Are Independent of Path"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bbc76e1-b401-5a78-abad-35dac56a605e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453342} {:answer/id #uuid "279f518b-43b4-54ff-a27b-f222f36cb0f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "279f518b-43b4-54ff-a27b-f222f36cb0f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453343} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ab559b0-8ad8-5600-af4d-58237670463b" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ traversed from $A$ to $B$ in counterclockwise direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454421} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2848ae05-afe6-565a-9e41-aea348ad8825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453344} {:answer/id #uuid "b066d196-4087-59b9-80a0-674602ceaaf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b066d196-4087-59b9-80a0-674602ceaaf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453345} :answer-field/id #uuid "029fd954-167e-57fe-8991-0827db39c02c" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the segment line $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454422} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa9edb55-47b4-5ffa-8f84-e71046dcce7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453346} {:answer/id #uuid "9b304306-6e7d-5cf9-b636-c3306a1cc7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa9edb55-47b4-5ffa-8f84-e71046dcce7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453346} :answer-field/id #uuid "1eb5c926-ae08-5e20-a8c6-c74a02337973" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454423} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2382595d-1329-5487-addb-48a96fc302ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453348} {:answer/id #uuid "ccaebe90-5c00-5752-8300-47cb5c96cc81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2382595d-1329-5487-addb-48a96fc302ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453348} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0ae2286-b965-58b3-9eee-07c2cde691c4" :answer-field/key "$F$ is conservative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b47df0de-b5ee-5562-b36a-a659cbe48d85" :question/math-academy-id "q-125796" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,x⟩$ and the points $A(0,1)$ and $B(0,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ traversed from $A$ to $B$ in counterclockwise direction” is true. Parameterizing the curve, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{1}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =t{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\pi  \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the segment line $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$” is true. Parameterizing the line segment, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{2}(t)=⟨0,\\,1-2t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨2t-1,\\,0⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}0\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path” is false. Since ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ have the same initial and terminal points, yet\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$\n\nwe conclude that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is path-dependent.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is conservative” is false. If a vector field is conservative then it is path-independent. Since $F$ is path-dependent, it is not conservative."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f0a57c2-bbad-5225-976b-385c7f117738" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Poisson Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fafa6def-aaf0-5ba2-855c-6a88e1f98666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473476} {:answer/id #uuid "9cffd3ba-fa84-5eda-ba42-26c885538925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cffd3ba-fa84-5eda-ba42-26c885538925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473477} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f6f9e92-f6eb-5e16-95a6-ac6d24f9d0fc" :answer-field/key "The number of defective televisions manufactured by a company in a month" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474133} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "865622aa-785a-5b05-a137-92c819638a38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473478} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2bf294-1137-5b80-afa9-26772372ac23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "865622aa-785a-5b05-a137-92c819638a38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473478} :answer-field/id #uuid "342ccc83-3967-547e-9cab-cc434f9e2c2c" :answer-field/key "The grade point average of a college class" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474134} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7ee65b5-ce94-51fe-8651-5731970a197c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473480} {:answer/id #uuid "046ed873-5824-5cf3-92bd-4a8300a4269a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7ee65b5-ce94-51fe-8651-5731970a197c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473480} :answer-field/id #uuid "9019b7d6-83fb-5a8e-9381-2f56267cbd57" :answer-field/key "The average speed of a car during a trip" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2963275e-8991-5613-bcc4-d15bd0b82d44" :question/math-academy-id "q-85317" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled using a Poisson distribution?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Poisson distribution models the number of events that occur in an interval of time or space if events occur independently and at a constant average rate.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable “The number of defective televisions manufactured by a company in a month” follows a Poisson distribution. The number of defective televisions can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a month).\n\n- Random variable “The grade point average of a college class” does *not* follow a Poisson distribution. The grade point average of a college class is not an event that occurs at a constant average rate.\n\n- Random variable “The average speed of a car during a trip” does *not* follow a Poisson distribution. The average speed of a car is not an event that occurs at a constant average rate.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The number of defective televisions manufactured by a company in a month” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f0a57c2-bbad-5225-976b-385c7f117738" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Poisson Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45d1f6bd-0673-5376-8af9-3c5ba94f3cf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472676} {:answer/id #uuid "02d1efff-26c9-52ad-8373-c552e7a54978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02d1efff-26c9-52ad-8373-c552e7a54978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472677} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6fe1ad9-de62-5bbe-a791-134fd8b89e33" :answer-field/key "The number of network failures per week" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473733} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdb89ed7-bf41-5376-be25-78ba840add8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472678} {:answer/id #uuid "d5ad5a80-3215-5093-9755-feb0f95130cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5ad5a80-3215-5093-9755-feb0f95130cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472679} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddca49c1-424d-55e8-b92c-b6e6d9fe90fc" :answer-field/key "The number of emergency calls received by a hospital every minute" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473734} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e33456e-379f-5dd8-803d-562fa5d1aefe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472680} {:answer/id #uuid "4f1976dc-6724-5c83-a696-cccb5b4d3a2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e33456e-379f-5dd8-803d-562fa5d1aefe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472680} :answer-field/id #uuid "60ef36e5-3c06-58f7-856f-d4155cb53598" :answer-field/key "The number of members of a band" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a75eec7-e20c-53a7-afe2-6cf4faf6becf" :question/math-academy-id "q-131311" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled using a Poisson distribution?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Poisson distribution models the number of events that occur in an interval of time or space if events occur independently and at a constant average rate.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable “The number of network failures per week” follows a Poisson distribution. The number of network failures can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a week).\n\n- Random variable “The number of emergency calls received by a hospital every minute” follows a Poisson distribution.  The number of emergency calls received can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a minute).\n\n- Random variable “The number of members of a band” does *not* follow a Poisson distribution. There are no events that occur at a constant average rate, and there is no interval of time or space.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The number of network failures per week”; “The number of emergency calls received by a hospital every minute” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f0a57c2-bbad-5225-976b-385c7f117738" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Poisson Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "904898ac-a1aa-5334-a804-a603ad8c7ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473524} {:answer/id #uuid "1ffe1232-4b50-5581-8a64-333584ee6cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ffe1232-4b50-5581-8a64-333584ee6cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473525} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a4727c7-b1c7-5992-8873-688025ef4125" :answer-field/key "The number of emails received by a company's server in one week" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474157} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec660059-5646-5b80-a137-eb74f5be8e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473526} {:answer/id #uuid "1bd3a2f5-2017-5804-8be3-c6c308862e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bd3a2f5-2017-5804-8be3-c6c308862e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473527} :answer-field/id #uuid "db746848-d7f2-5e73-a8dc-b141e9015e73" :answer-field/key "The number of people who visit a coffee shop per hour" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474158} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff68197e-68ef-5efc-b00e-7a0963f51a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473528} {:answer/id #uuid "55129bd0-7867-555a-9be8-808e4d31da4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff68197e-68ef-5efc-b00e-7a0963f51a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473528} :answer-field/id #uuid "64d74df4-c3ba-59a9-afc8-fdf98329aaae" :answer-field/key "The height of $5$ buildings in New York City" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71278ae0-44f4-58f6-827b-4b9773ebb613" :question/math-academy-id "q-89222" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled using a Poisson distribution?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Poisson distribution models the number of events that occur in an interval of time or space if events occur independently and at a constant average rate.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable “The number of emails received by a company's server in one week” follows a Poisson distribution. The number of emails received by a company's server can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (one week).\n\n- Random variable “The number of people who visit a coffee shop per hour” follows a Poisson distribution. The number of people who visit a coffee shop can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (one hour).\n\n- Random variable “The height of $5$ buildings in New York City” does *not* follow a Poisson distribution. There are no events that occur at a constant average rate, and there is no interval of time or space.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The number of emails received by a company's server in one week”; “The number of people who visit a coffee shop per hour” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f0a57c2-bbad-5225-976b-385c7f117738" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Poisson Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a92e176d-3955-50fe-8147-44d2a591c6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472682} {:answer/id #uuid "d3604c50-1e5e-5384-a961-8aa6a3eae304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a92e176d-3955-50fe-8147-44d2a591c6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472682} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b72f2bc-c09e-5bc5-885c-add4964c9b74" :answer-field/key "The average points scored on a math test in a class" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e369d76-1aae-55c7-a19d-61ffb59a914d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472684} {:answer/id #uuid "74afb83a-49b6-596f-9e6e-13eaafaa523a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74afb83a-49b6-596f-9e6e-13eaafaa523a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472685} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d7133b9-872a-5415-94ac-9f2d37cbf978" :answer-field/key "The number of orders a firm receives per month" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473737} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "274444d5-1cad-58d7-9af5-8bc7a59aa017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472686} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7d01b4-199a-5d1b-80a4-1f3aef59ace1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d7d01b4-199a-5d1b-80a4-1f3aef59ace1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472687} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d9fb68-3ffe-5c1a-bd34-30b76a78e7bf" :answer-field/key "The number of calls a firm will receive next week for help concerning a toy" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a68d38c1-253b-59e6-ad1e-93208422e4e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-131412" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled using a Poisson distribution?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Poisson distribution models the number of events that occur in an interval of time or space if events occur independently and at a constant average rate.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable “The average points scored on a math test in a class” does *not* follow a Poisson distribution. The average points scored on the math test is not an event that occurs at a constant average rate.\n\n- Random variable “The number of orders a firm receives per month” follows a Poisson distribution. The number of orders can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a month).\n\n- Random variable “The number of calls a firm will receive next week for help concerning a toy” follows a Poisson distribution. Again, the number of calls can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a week).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The number of orders a firm receives per month”; “The number of calls a firm will receive next week for help concerning a toy” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f0a57c2-bbad-5225-976b-385c7f117738" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Poisson Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a83b8bf-f148-5771-ab62-abc8a88c89c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473470} {:answer/id #uuid "200b2717-b678-52c8-a38b-dcc7faf7cd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "200b2717-b678-52c8-a38b-dcc7faf7cd82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text}