checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d411b05d-363a-5c38-b187-cabf795e2dff" :question/math-academy-id "q-85316" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled using a Poisson distribution?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Poisson distribution models the number of events that occur in an interval of time or space if events occur independently and at a constant average rate.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable “The number of visits a web page has per minute” follows a Poisson distribution. The number of visits on a web page can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a minute).\n\n- Random variable “The number of works of art created by a sculptor in a period of one year” follows a Poisson distribution. The number of works of art can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (a year).\n\n- Random variable “The average height of the players on a basketball team” does *not* follow a Poisson distribution. There are no events that occur at a constant average rate, and there is no interval of time or space.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The number of visits a web page has per minute”; “The number of works of art created by a sculptor in a period of one year” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04e719c2-0320-5791-b983-6b439ef537de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472856} {:answer/id #uuid "6c0b13a1-62f1-5553-bcbd-448f6af6e81a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c0b13a1-62f1-5553-bcbd-448f6af6e81a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472857} :answer-field/id #uuid "7659e378-9a5a-5e51-9c6b-123e8db92f8c" :answer-field/key "$n=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cc110b0-980a-5da9-a368-1d441f2e14e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472858} {:answer/id #uuid "23cabb60-197b-58d3-b057-a401c9b60c3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23cabb60-197b-58d3-b057-a401c9b60c3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472859} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff5bb257-fc6a-5969-bd76-b2f265fb880a" :answer-field/key "$n=9$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e7fcce6-9840-5474-ac13-57b36e28e608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472860} {:answer/id #uuid "802680a9-a6a4-5def-9609-d2a7a40f477f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e7fcce6-9840-5474-ac13-57b36e28e608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472860} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ecee75d-11c5-5fba-8893-0cddff0394f7" :answer-field/key "$n=12$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "237ee44c-ddeb-50a9-b28f-87d4edfa4e60" :question/math-academy-id "q-212521" :question/problem "Given that $-21≡-12\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=-21-(-12)=-9.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $3∣(-9)$ because $(-9)÷3=-3,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=3.$\n\n- Note that $9∣(-9)$ because $(-9)÷9=-1,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=9.$\n\n- Note that $12∤(-9).$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=12.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $n=3$; $n=9$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152075 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a07c5ec7-8199-53c7-9738-80e360d03b38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Modulus"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b22152ce-58df-5d5c-a9a7-ba02352c55aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473338} {:answer/id #uuid "076c6326-e56f-5a55-8cce-576ee8ff3ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "076c6326-e56f-5a55-8cce-576ee8ff3ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473339} :answer-field/id #uuid "53684faa-202a-5928-b132-14a5034a255a" :answer-field/key "$n=7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474064} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80af74f8-1f7d-51ed-b670-9aaae0e5d2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473340} {:answer/id #uuid "25113294-a512-5863-9023-b0167b7c809f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80af74f8-1f7d-51ed-b670-9aaae0e5d2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473340} :answer-field/id #uuid "3777b970-73d5-5c49-89c5-8d64d21f5000" :answer-field/key "$n=9$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9163e2b9-954f-5fd6-b2fe-291b223e344c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473342} {:answer/id #uuid "8e501603-638e-55de-adf9-ab132ae2ca0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e501603-638e-55de-adf9-ab132ae2ca0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473343} :answer-field/id #uuid "d013da85-465d-5629-92e9-fa4b42ff4a9a" :answer-field/key "$n=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7dad68af-5609-5774-82ac-907f4e4304f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-76962" :question/problem "Given that $19≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),$ which of the following could be the value of $n?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWe have $a-b=19-5=14.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Note that $7∣14$ because $14÷7=2,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=7.$\n\n- Note that $9∤14.$ Therefore, the statement is false when $n=9.$\n\n- Note that $2∣14$ because $14÷2=7,$ and there is no remainder. Therefore, the statement is true when $n=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $n=7$; $n=2$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eebe007-8a95-578d-b553-e37a7bd8a327" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cd7a5c1-1e87-5b62-b284-bf56909fcf02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453114} {:answer/id #uuid "cd253dba-c992-5d6a-93f7-47cc0eff8bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cd7a5c1-1e87-5b62-b284-bf56909fcf02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453114} :answer-field/id #uuid "1238bba7-07b2-559e-bf74-19e6124b8f75" :answer-field/key "$-7≡27\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454307} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6ab698b-ceeb-5deb-8953-08cf2d434ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453116} {:answer/id #uuid "3c93d61c-1738-5e36-85b9-dac6be86a64e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6ab698b-ceeb-5deb-8953-08cf2d434ca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453116} :answer-field/id #uuid "4003b46e-ef87-59a5-8fe4-e94a66c5b3e9" :answer-field/key "$-5≡15\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454308} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bff6d71-cd27-5c11-ba51-8d4d2bd41fe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453118} {:answer/id #uuid "de862315-e733-5ab2-b08c-faee53b6da8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de862315-e733-5ab2-b08c-faee53b6da8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453119} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f6a383b-7b94-51a2-896a-27d32fdf2e42" :answer-field/key "$11≡18\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c37fbba7-25b2-5279-9899-188d8dedca8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-103380" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-7≡27\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$ is false because $5∤(-7-27).$ Notice that $-7-27=-34,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\n- Statement $-5≡15\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ is false because $6∤(-5-15).$ Notice that $-5-15=-20,$ which is not divisible by $6.$\n\n- Statement $11≡18\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ is true because $7\\,|\\,(11-18).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(11-18)÷7=-7÷7=-1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $11≡18\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eebe007-8a95-578d-b553-e37a7bd8a327" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ded5d75d-d5af-5618-8bc9-286fd9df75b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453294} {:answer/id #uuid "9a2e7b64-9936-5f01-9f31-27b68303212b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ded5d75d-d5af-5618-8bc9-286fd9df75b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453294} :answer-field/id #uuid "abebb316-e99d-5b7e-85e8-d421aa3b8c60" :answer-field/key "$-5≡8\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454397} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ad2655f-6afb-58dd-bfd3-1cab2b3512c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453296} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ffcbf0-fd13-59c6-8328-9a3f78249d1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7ffcbf0-fd13-59c6-8328-9a3f78249d1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453297} :answer-field/id #uuid "16e50a4a-182e-53b4-ab0f-3c14cfb5c41c" :answer-field/key "$-23≡-5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454398} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3f32310-cea6-56fd-bc90-91e2d05d76f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453298} {:answer/id #uuid "a622ca61-c74d-526d-a675-f91fa6ed458a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a622ca61-c74d-526d-a675-f91fa6ed458a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453299} :answer-field/id #uuid "52acd980-54ed-5661-a99d-d100f4fdb7da" :answer-field/key "$-7≡-1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454399}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9350880-d00e-5d41-adb3-52fc6c8e0846" :question/math-academy-id "q-113664" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-5≡8\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ is false because $7∤(-5-8).$ Notice that $-5-8=-13,$ which is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- Statement $-23≡-5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$ is true because $6∣(-23-(-5)).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-23-(-5))÷6=-18÷6=-3\n$$\n\n- Statement $-7≡-1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$ is true because $2\\,|\\,(-7-(-1)).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-7-(-1))÷2=-6÷2=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-23≡-5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$; $-7≡-1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2eebe007-8a95-578d-b553-e37a7bd8a327" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fea04ad-6301-5338-84cb-8e7183ec38b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453300} {:answer/id #uuid "244b0170-04cf-576a-a359-8e6fba1609a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fea04ad-6301-5338-84cb-8e7183ec38b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453300} :answer-field/id #uuid "294256a8-04dd-5480-bd9a-025d2d07c052" :answer-field/key "$-36≡-19\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454400} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce7da18-5976-54f4-853e-11cd748582b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453302} {:answer/id #uuid "d63a67dc-af8b-597d-8d04-bea8356b228f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ce7da18-5976-54f4-853e-11cd748582b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453302} :answer-field/id #uuid "831851a3-f614-56ed-a446-b0ef1f20f1be" :answer-field/key "$15≡-26\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454401} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f172228e-e7ef-5590-9ed8-ef46152687d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453304} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4882f8-d7db-52e7-a801-2733051a47c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc4882f8-d7db-52e7-a801-2733051a47c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453305} :answer-field/id #uuid "236f2576-4c98-5799-8b90-5d928320dac1" :answer-field/key "$-27≡9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ee3460a5-a9ce-5793-8247-ccd3db242273" :question/math-academy-id "q-113675" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-36≡-19\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ is false because $7∤(-36-(-19)).$ Notice that $-36-(-19)=-17,$ which is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- Statement $15≡-26\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)$ is false because $10∤(15-(-26)).$ Notice that $15-(-26)=41,$ which is not divisible by $10.$\n\n- Statement $-27≡9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$ is true because $4\\,|\\,(-27-9).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-27-9)÷4=-36÷4=-9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-27≡9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419686 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connections Between Matrices of a Linear Transformation Relative to Different Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "573ba886-20ef-53c9-9024-a795a327b2ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454244} {:answer/id #uuid "75fa156d-1a39-536a-ab92-cd46c3d568a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75fa156d-1a39-536a-ab92-cd46c3d568a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454245} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c352d4a-a883-55eb-8913-4568682a7132" :answer-field/key "$[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a493b3a0-15e1-540d-9b9a-49e179799c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454246} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0b13f5-b674-5518-b581-93c06913cf58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a493b3a0-15e1-540d-9b9a-49e179799c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454246} :answer-field/id #uuid "139440a5-d4e1-5ab8-ba4c-c3d86f2c0c74" :answer-field/key "$[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454873} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41af9a8e-a9d1-5b00-b3e8-b95a4c022fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454248} {:answer/id #uuid "3a437d50-f3c9-5ac5-8e9a-de9b7e0b61f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a437d50-f3c9-5ac5-8e9a-de9b7e0b61f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454249} :answer-field/id #uuid "08c42cdc-f60a-5dff-99c5-7c1367615b5d" :answer-field/key "$[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e737a421-d643-51f0-9d67-b9556fcc15c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-97060" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$; $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "559e653a-2ab9-54a8-84e3-02bf106a8f47" :knowledge-point/title "Inferring Divisibility in Algebraic Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c2f8bfc-8a2b-5c27-8a60-ea04aa4bdc5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453806} {:answer/id #uuid "999777ab-3743-55c2-a473-e80ef89adb78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c2f8bfc-8a2b-5c27-8a60-ea04aa4bdc5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453806} :answer-field/id #uuid "782c3be1-ac75-5aa2-b432-a55b29c6fd04" :answer-field/key "$3∣(14x+21y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454653} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcbbbb8b-969a-59eb-ad64-12cbd15b1875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453808} {:answer/id #uuid "817d5feb-1d83-5247-bbc1-274b57d7c67d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "817d5feb-1d83-5247-bbc1-274b57d7c67d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453809} :answer-field/id #uuid "60099b3d-b168-5c08-9592-0c6035c14b35" :answer-field/key "$7∣(14x+21y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454654} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ad412ec-4d05-534c-98e0-999e777f75f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453810} {:answer/id #uuid "f0567f6e-4237-5109-82cc-40dfbc24f6ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ad412ec-4d05-534c-98e0-999e777f75f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453810} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d462da8-c335-5522-ab67-992c40543616" :answer-field/key "$4∣(14x+21y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "48fbd1ea-16f2-572a-98a1-c1983af51b24" :question/math-academy-id "q-221923" :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $3∣(14x+21y)$ is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $14(1)+21(0)=14,$ which is not divisible by $3.$\n\n- Statement $7∣(14x+21y)$ is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n14x+21y=7(2x+3y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $2x+3y$ must be an integer, too. So, $7∣(14x+21y).$\n\n- Statement $4∣(14x+21y)$ is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $14(1)+21(0)=14,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $7∣(14x+21y)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420072 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161919 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "559e653a-2ab9-54a8-84e3-02bf106a8f47" :knowledge-point/title "Inferring Divisibility in Algebraic Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a14c4a6-d210-5dd4-9ce2-f9ed55f64943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453830} {:answer/id #uuid "287bceee-04d3-509d-acda-bcc302b3c7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "287bceee-04d3-509d-acda-bcc302b3c7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453831} :answer-field/id #uuid "f65bdc06-29ae-5226-b267-6fdc35815932" :answer-field/key "$2$ divides $(6x-18y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dcb7a7e-04a6-5748-90a8-7d2a33acd246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453832} {:answer/id #uuid "4905546e-c0ac-5cb3-afe1-6534073d8055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4905546e-c0ac-5cb3-afe1-6534073d8055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453833} :answer-field/id #uuid "0638118a-1557-568f-9f04-35cd1542f5a3" :answer-field/key "$3$ divides $(6x-18y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e78ce48-c819-5bbc-bd9f-602a454f17b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453834} {:answer/id #uuid "76454f66-2d6e-5f8a-85c0-8183da34db1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e78ce48-c819-5bbc-bd9f-602a454f17b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453834} :answer-field/id #uuid "00285ea7-c2b8-59c7-a9e9-3de805e315c4" :answer-field/key "$5$ divides $(6x-18y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63936aa1-e722-5014-a82a-6fe76f4b851d" :question/math-academy-id "q-221929" :question/problem "Which of the following statements must be true for any integers $x$ and $y?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$2$ divides $(6x-18y)$” is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n6x-18y=2(3x-9y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $3x-9y$ must be an integer, too. So, $2$ divides $(6x-18y).$\n\n- Statement “$3$ divides $(6x-18y)$” is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n6x-18y=3(2x-6y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $2x-6y$ must be an integer, too. So, $3$ divides $(6x-18y).$\n\n- Statement “$5$ divides $(6x-18y)$” is false. For example, if $x=2$ and $y=1,$ we have $6(2)-18(1)=-6,$ which is not divisible by $5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$2$ divides $(6x-18y)$”; “$3$ divides $(6x-18y)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092223 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b86558a-4c99-5ccb-a100-719692a056f4" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Matrix That Represents a Rotation of 90 Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29c4d9e7-fcc1-51cb-9feb-d14eed398feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472754} {:answer/id #uuid "48e4a354-249b-5ba2-9117-b2967ef925f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48e4a354-249b-5ba2-9117-b2967ef925f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472755} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd5de993-b98b-510c-aca5-b262d4fe57ab" :answer-field/key "The point $(3,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2776862c-c124-5cdd-a3a8-95305ed05171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472756} {:answer/id #uuid "ff8c4bf0-30a7-5205-a922-7ff4168cd4ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2776862c-c124-5cdd-a3a8-95305ed05171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472756} :answer-field/id #uuid "7496452b-de20-5cb6-96eb-ad9d02d388c8" :answer-field/key "The point $(2,-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473773} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b9e0b92-1b40-59a0-a102-0725a2933668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472758} {:answer/id #uuid "685a4b07-2685-5bcc-833d-6284d65a3096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "685a4b07-2685-5bcc-833d-6284d65a3096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472759} :answer-field/id #uuid "869b058e-5f7d-52b3-ba22-dde49434dad4" :answer-field/key "The point $(-4,-1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "08bf8696-2d24-58a9-b5b4-856286859054" :question/math-academy-id "q-160646" :question/problem "A triangle $S$ has vertices at  $(-1,3),(-2,2),(1,-4).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${90}^{∘}$ is the same as counterclockwise rotation by an angle of ${270}^{∘}.$ It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-{90}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(3,1),(2,2),(-4,-1).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(3,1)$”; “The point $(-4,-1)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420258 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198309 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb430d5-5241-56a2-96be-73f44b0f2114" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Transitivity of Divisibility"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a19b88d-f0d3-5ce1-a354-e16dd44157c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453800} {:answer/id #uuid "0b541dca-6c1b-51ea-8ff8-8e8c09c289b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a19b88d-f0d3-5ce1-a354-e16dd44157c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453800} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1b4e2c7-01ac-5098-b14e-68597e290a8c" :answer-field/key "If $11∣k$ then $33∣k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454650} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78cf09bc-6b7f-591c-abaf-c9751546fdb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453802} {:answer/id #uuid "ddeb9d9e-70bb-5940-bdfd-2a3d6e2e6eeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddeb9d9e-70bb-5940-bdfd-2a3d6e2e6eeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453803} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8c07ba5-b2aa-5743-8686-116a9dcce74f" :answer-field/key "If $33∣k$ then $11∣k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454651} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f827277c-b111-5abf-97a9-9696bb10ca2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453804} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e904d9-1ffd-59fc-8e5a-55e88cc383fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0e904d9-1ffd-59fc-8e5a-55e88cc383fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453805} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aee165a-37d1-5d6a-ac3d-2a33ddf9b389" :answer-field/key "If $33∣k$ then $3∣k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454652}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24815c66-50ab-5aab-ac7b-25ddc673e132" :question/math-academy-id "q-221381" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$ we have transitivity of divisibility:\n\n$a∣b\\,$ and $\\,b∣c$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $a∣c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement “If $11∣k$ then $33∣k$” is false. As a counterexample, let $k=11.$ Then, $11∣11$ but $33∤11.$\n\n- Statement “If $33∣k$ then $11∣k$” is true. First, note that $11∣33.$ Therefore, we have\n$11∣33$ and $33∣k,$ which implies that $11∣k.$\n\n- Statement “If $33∣k$ then $3∣k$” is true. First, note that $3∣33.$ Therefore, we have\n$3∣33$ and $33∣k,$ which implies that $3∣k.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $33∣k$ then $11∣k$”; “If $33∣k$ then $3∣k$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420260 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198310 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b3101aa-ee9e-5940-b170-2f4e78802150" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Divisibility of a Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af754b47-d4e5-5fdc-8bd2-d6344c3485f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454108} {:answer/id #uuid "20675c10-e23b-542e-8faa-3a28254d9e8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20675c10-e23b-542e-8faa-3a28254d9e8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454109} :answer-field/id #uuid "e07d4f8b-55b6-5aab-b645-ac6b2ab28954" :answer-field/key "If $10\\,|\\,21b$ then $10\\,|\\,b$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454804} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7366dfaa-c59f-53f8-9c22-adfa0d5da165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454110} {:answer/id #uuid "b9dda14e-0c1b-50ef-9d7b-3b7da9a958ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9dda14e-0c1b-50ef-9d7b-3b7da9a958ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454111} :answer-field/id #uuid "52e80153-dfde-514d-9bca-409913cc19fb" :answer-field/key "If $21\\,|\\,25b$ then $21\\,|\\,b$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "933f0836-d1bf-5067-a251-88602fe68e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454112} {:answer/id #uuid "a54ed7bb-eae7-5c80-b6d8-e0ca1356ae7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "933f0836-d1bf-5067-a251-88602fe68e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454112} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fa5cf00-ada4-5c14-974f-fda0ade37b37" :answer-field/key "If $15\\,|\\,9b$ then $15\\,|\\,b$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42a248b1-4b2a-5a7f-b673-589ac28da9a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-93649" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement “If $10\\,|\\,21b$ then $10\\,|\\,b$” is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(10,21)=1.$ Therefore, we have $10\\,|\\,21b$ and $\\text{gcd}(10,21)=1,$ which implies $10\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement “If $21\\,|\\,25b$ then $21\\,|\\,b$” is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(21,25)=1.$ Therefore, we have $21\\,|\\,25b$ and $\\text{gcd}(21,25)=1,$ which implies $21\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement “If $15\\,|\\,9b$ then $15\\,|\\,b$” is false. As a counterexample, let $b=5.$ Then, $15∣9\\cdot 5$ but $15∤5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $10\\,|\\,21b$ then $10\\,|\\,b$”; “If $21\\,|\\,25b$ then $21\\,|\\,b$” only."} 