wer/id #uuid "b1521e88-f7fe-5024-9ad1-4e80a1f3ef2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454118} {:answer/id #uuid "471b8f3e-0e11-5794-b4e9-d0565d0ed717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "471b8f3e-0e11-5794-b4e9-d0565d0ed717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454119} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ee8f5f6-b6e7-5ae4-8c2d-b577fba2c54a" :answer-field/key "If $22\\,|\\,{7}^{2}b$ then $22\\,|\\,b$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "553ed68f-8e74-5dda-a8b3-cdd3e89c31cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-93650" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement “If ${19}^{2}\\,|\\,19b$ then ${19}^{2}\\,|\\,b$” is false. As a counterexample, let $b=19.$ Then, ${19}^{2}∣19\\cdot 19$ but ${19}^{2}∤19.$\n\n- Statement “If $12\\,|\\,35b$ then $12\\,|\\,b$” is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(12,35)=1.$ Therefore, we have $12\\,|\\,35b$ and $\\text{gcd}(12,35)=1,$ which implies $12\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement “If $22\\,|\\,{7}^{2}b$ then $22\\,|\\,b$” is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(22,{7}^{2})=1.$ Therefore, we have $22\\,|\\,{7}^{2}b$ and $\\text{gcd}(22,{7}^{2})=1,$ which implies $22\\,|\\,b.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $12\\,|\\,35b$ then $12\\,|\\,b$”; “If $22\\,|\\,{7}^{2}b$ then $22\\,|\\,b$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 1759