/ref 17592186453645} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d280a24-a16d-5b3b-963f-bb375f7da8e5" :answer-field/key "$l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines is a **sufficient** condition for $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454572} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005f66ed-8f1a-52f9-827d-2d2e267ad68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453646} {:answer/id #uuid "e960af39-d3a3-5f17-8c2f-2ad92f587599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "005f66ed-8f1a-52f9-827d-2d2e267ad68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453646} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf101830-7404-5e46-b7dd-1e4d16a0cbf7" :answer-field/key "$l\\cap m\\ne ∅$ is a **sufficient** condition for $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bbf3a4e-b9b9-5f74-9d97-2501c2b02398" :question/math-academy-id "q-183393" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $l$ and $m$ are coplanar and perpendicular lines, then $l\\cap m\\ne ∅.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the implication above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(\\,l,m\\text{ are coplanar and perpendicular lines}\\,)}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,\\underbrace{(\\,l\\cap m\\ne ∅\\,)}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement “$l\\cap m\\ne ∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines” is true. $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines\n\n- Statement “$l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines is a **sufficient** condition for $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$” is true. $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines is a **sufficient** condition for $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$l\\cap m\\ne ∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines”; “$l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines is a **sufficient** condition for $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152077 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bc3ecd-2da1-5951-abba-95da02dee826" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e2e3884-4256-5fcd-a5d4-dadd9c5c4fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474508} {:answer/id #uuid "99a25cfb-7af1-584e-a23f-07d1873c1ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e2e3884-4256-5fcd-a5d4-dadd9c5c4fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474508} :answer-field/id #uuid "16abb1e1-f335-5e47-9697-b110c37be556" :answer-field/key "$x>4$" :