ed that $P$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option “Whenever $x=0,$ then ${x}^{2}=x$” reads\n\n$$\n\\text{Whenever}\\,\\underbrace{x=0\\text{,}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{then}\\,\\underbrace{{x}^{2}=x}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option “${x}^{2}=x$ whenever $x=0$” reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{x}^{2}=x}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{whenever}\\,\\underbrace{x=0}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option “$x=0,$ provided that ${x}^{2}=x$” reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x=0\\text{,}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{provided that}\\,\\underbrace{{x}^{2}=x}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “Whenever $x=0,$ then ${x}^{2}=x$”; “${x}^{2}=x$ whenever $x=0$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e66005fe-df33-590a-9d9c-91947cd4a608" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Fundamental Sets of Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efc36190-e9b2-59a8-90c3-e42746b56e48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474756} {:answer/id #uuid "64273c85-b54b-59a4-85ac-81ca202e2b07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64273c85-b54b-59a4-85ac-81ca202e2b07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474757} :answer-field/id #uuid "f069e89d-9efc-5468-a700-6f1c190427d9" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=x$ is a solution to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475304} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c223e50-374d-53fb-9ef7-5a76d425cc83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474758} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd04d69-7309-5a80-8141-f52da0de1b60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c223e50-374d-53fb-9ef7-5a76d425cc83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474758} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c72983f-bc9a-5d8a-a9d9-c1192271f6a9" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{2}$ is a solution to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475305} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "849b82db-c774-5be6-b08a-ea48ead49bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474760} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a3326f-c419-5d83-add3-70561f8b99a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "849b82db-c774-5be6-b08a-ea48ead49bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474760} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ef9fe9d-abab-5748-a003-4777d555bb38" :answer-field/key "The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475306}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46d6b627-57fc-5c4f-9c8a-dc31a7241e7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334252" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that to determine whether $y(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute $y$ and its derivatives into the equation. \n\nLet's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{1}(x)=x$ is a solution to the equation” is true. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{1}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =1 \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}(0)-x(1)+x & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{2}$ is a solution to the equation” is false. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{2}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =2x \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}(2)-x(2x)+{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}(x)$ is not a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation” is false. Since ${y}_{2}(x)$ is not a solution of the given differential equation, ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ don't form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${y}_{1}(x)=x$ is a solution to the equation” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d074dea2-9b08-51ae-a12c-baf0473ca84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474626} {:answer/id #uuid "0745ed52-86ba-5e86-a9f5-e70229ac22d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d074dea2-9b08-51ae-a12c-baf0473ca84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474626} :answer-field/id #uuid "be2ebc52-7384-5d75-816e-60c49a6a2fe5" :answer-field/key "$A⊄B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475239} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf4b3440-fc76-5da9-8a1a-101b60935d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474628} {:answer/id #uuid "6b07da64-c759-539c-8822-0100ac81394d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf4b3440-fc76-5da9-8a1a-101b60935d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474628} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0c4e0ec-4e6b-5624-b84a-752ef7179b7c" :answer-field/key "$|A|\\ne |B|$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475240} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7dd4394-62d9-59bb-a2a5-c6d2cefe8b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474630} {:answer/id #uuid "4763b50f-c918-5bd1-93e4-4aa362986b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7dd4394-62d9-59bb-a2a5-c6d2cefe8b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474630} :answer-field/id #uuid "5844b7a0-ee09-5afb-98cc-df9699b3870d" :answer-field/key "$A⊇B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c07a7ee-9fb6-5236-b864-38ec61e9b0cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-214241" :question/problem "Which of the following are equivalence relations on $P(N)?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- The relation \"$⊄$\" is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not symmetric since ${2,3}⊄{2}$ but ${2}⊂{2,3}.$\n\n- The relation \"$\\ne $\" for the cardinalities of sets is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive since $|{2}|=|{2}|.$\n\n- The relation \"$⊇$\" is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not symmetric since $N⊇{1}$ but ${1}⊉N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46304a09-231c-5b25-b0af-6bef3091dcec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474864} {:answer/id #uuid "749b5fd3-d7f2-55a2-b00b-2ce2da4d8942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46304a09-231c-5b25-b0af-6bef3091dcec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474864} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fcfb08e-a2ba-546d-a6de-91285cdc2c98" :answer-field/key "$x\\,R\\,y$ if $xy>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475358} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d93d11d-3bed-56c4-a65c-f4d82c22cc5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474866} {:answer/id #uuid "6619aa66-ee00-5c0f-a2fc-107f13599e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d93d11d-3bed-56c4-a65c-f4d82c22cc5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474866} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b574e14-003c-551e-ac09-7810a6d70b59" :answer-field/key "$x\\,R\\,y$ if $x=2y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2160c789-1c39-5adf-a0e1-cdb6a5dccfff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474868} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c97f8a-9fc3-5be7-b455-69f584cbd7bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6c97f8a-9fc3-5be7-b455-69f584cbd7bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474869} :answer-field/id #uuid "90379e7a-559f-528b-a0b8-41ba0277a88c" :answer-field/key "$x\\,R\\,y$ if $x-y$ is a rational number" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a65003f-5b78-57dd-8ad6-282231fb787b" :question/math-academy-id "q-76164" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are equivalence relations on $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- Relation “$x\\,R\\,y$ if $xy>0$” is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because $0\\cdot 0=0≯0.$\n\n- Relation “$x\\,R\\,y$ if $x=2y$” is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not symmetric because $2=2(1)$ but $1\\ne 2(2).$\n\n- Relation “$x\\,R\\,y$ if $x-y$ is a rational number” is an equivalence relation:\n\n- It is reflexive because for all $x\\in R,$ we have $x-x=0$ is a rational number.\n\n- It is symmetric because for all $x,y\\in R,$ if $x-y=r$ is a rational number, then $y-x=-(x-y)=-r$ is also a rational number.\n\n- It is transitive because for all $x,y,z\\in R,$ if $x-y=r$ and $y-z=q,$ where $r,q$ are rational numbers, then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-z=(x-y)+(y-z)=r+q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis also a rational number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$x\\,R\\,y$ if $x-y$ is a rational number” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b70dd396-b01a-51e6-a52c-8ff729f48c45" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Standard Relation Is an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d2ecaf5-e9a0-5ac2-9183-69db4543a66a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453742} {:answer/id #uuid "9c2e347c-bbd6-5423-9565-80267bb6eaab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c2e347c-bbd6-5423-9565-80267bb6eaab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453743} :answer-field/id #uuid "57f53dd6-66c3-5316-bb4d-346cf5f0671c" :answer-field/key "$R$ is reflexive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454621} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "369ec3ac-7594-53e7-86b1-8ed81e593cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453744} {:answer/id #uuid "ece1440a-f636-5a14-bd79-3859bd270e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ece1440a-f636-5a14-bd79-3859bd270e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453745} :answer-field/id #uuid "8397c69c-e704-5336-ab46-63a2a420b12b" :answer-field/key "$R$ is symmetric" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454622} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cb40e47-129b-5e8c-96ec-f9dffe1c80b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453746} {:answer/id #uuid "78de381b-cb88-517b-9e8f-479328b7da2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78de381b-cb88-517b-9e8f-479328b7da2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453747} :answer-field/id #uuid "0424cae6-af37-5568-967e-b8349f54700c" :answer-field/key "$R$ is transitive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454623} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee7950d-2e0f-561b-a855-dcda433c326e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453748} {:answer/id #uuid "52ec55e9-022a-5936-b3fd-bf3dd4db01ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52ec55e9-022a-5936-b3fd-bf3dd4db01ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453749} :answer-field/id #uuid "347ab12e-5830-50c8-b5fe-11a0cb0e2867" :answer-field/key "$R$ is an equivalence relation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b086cc6-e229-5377-bb89-5a8ff879bb27" :question/math-academy-id "q-214271" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $P(A),$ where $A={1,2,3,…,10}.$ \n\n$$\nX\\,R\\,Y\\,⇔\\,|X|=|Y|\n$$\n\n Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive. For all $X\\in P(A),$ $|X|\\,=\\,|X|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric. For all $X,Y\\in P(A),$ if $|X|\\,=\\,|Y|,$ then $|Y|=|X|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive. For all $X,Y,Z\\in P(A),$ if $|X|=|Y|$ and $|Y|=|Z|,$ then $|X|=|Z|.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$R$ is reflexive”; “$R$ is symmetric”; “$R$ is transitive”; “$R$ is an equivalence relation” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421408 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e4c7950-28e5-5f87-b20d-5cd3ddc396fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474632} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ca370f-8fd4-5122-9efc-7caeca9460d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e4c7950-28e5-5f87-b20d-5cd3ddc396fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474632} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd1bd756-3043-5134-837d-147e1313e4e1" :answer-field/key "$A\\,R\\,B$ if $A\\cap B=∅$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c80d39e-eb35-5216-8249-21a7fefd55c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474634} {:answer/id #uuid "0d9691e1-4b06-59a2-b16c-2f78d16ab75a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c80d39e-eb35-5216-8249-21a7fefd55c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474634} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ec1fc92-6bb8-5a83-b40e-c88ee268298e" :answer-field/key "$A⊃B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475243} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c86aa1e7-9d83-5217-b905-1b9ecc274127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474636} {:answer/id #uuid "b90cb604-c027-5d2d-a431-39c452d530b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b90cb604-c027-5d2d-a431-39c452d530b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474637} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e038680-1141-5ab4-8488-09f225d6a567" :answer-field/key "$A=B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c8d639d-4ba9-5766-b837-cc9cfbce29a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-214245" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are equivalence relations on $P(N)?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- Relation “$A\\,R\\,B$ if $A\\cap B=∅$” is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because ${1}\\cap {1}\\ne ∅.$\n\n- Relation $A⊃B$ is also not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because ${1}⊅{1}.$\n\n- Relation $A=B$ is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A=B$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8a27e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations on Finite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ce48c9f-99d9-5a57-a00b-4e4bf360757e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453758} {:answer/id #uuid "14605bc1-af90-5790-a615-0b1a9fadf2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14605bc1-af90-5790-a615-0b1a9fadf2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453759} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e9fae93-f58a-52ee-974c-59c83db2d398" :answer-field/key "$R$ is reflexive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454629} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "210119e1-9f58-5f00-bcc7-6333b4e848ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453760} {:answer/id #uuid "b70ed475-e1f8-58ae-a66a-874ef7941e02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b70ed475-e1f8-58ae-a66a-874ef7941e02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453761} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7dd1b09-67f2-5d7e-8540-c20af79475a1" :answer-field/key "$R$ is symmetric" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454630} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "256f4a2d-29a4-53b4-ae5c-d7eb935aa6ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453762} {:answer/id #uuid "a4311142-cfe1-519d-a1fc-72dc161de438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4311142-cfe1-519d-a1fc-72dc161de438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453763} :answer-field/id #uuid "63b78ba8-15e8-5751-85dc-2bc2a2888d54" :answer-field/key "$R$ is transitive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454631} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7032d3cc-7d83-5d21-99fd-722fc4057579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453764} {:answer/id #uuid "023c0a2a-6bf5-54dd-90e6-ef95b2cf26d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "023c0a2a-6bf5-54dd-90e6-ef95b2cf26d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453765} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5d24233-3893-5769-9223-4fd5ac58fcdf" :answer-field/key "$R$ is an equivalence relation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ee391cd-217d-5ff1-a899-24ea6980b5eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-214279" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={∗,⋆,∘,⋄}$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(∗,∗),(⋆,⋆),(∘,∘),(⋄,⋄),(∗,⋆),(⋆,∗)}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(∗,∗),(⋆,⋆),(∘,∘),(⋄,⋄)\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive because for all $x,y,z\\in {∗,⋆,∘,⋄},$ if  $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,z)\\in R,$  then $(x,z)\\in R.$ Recall that it's sufficient to check only the cases when both pairs have different components: \n\n- $(∗,⋆)\\in R$ and $(⋆,∗)\\in R,$ and also $(∗,∗)\\in R$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $(⋆,∗)\\in R$ and $(∗,⋆)\\in R,$ and also $(⋆,⋆)\\in R$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Since $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, it is an equivalence relation.$\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$R$ is reflexive”; “$R$ is symmetric”; “$R$ is transitive”; “$R$ is an equivalence relation”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8a27e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations on Finite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f596310-0e1c-53ef-9f1c-67543d48af1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474658} {:answer/id #uuid "d1bab53c-7396-5e9f-8554-262f35c8714b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f596310-0e1c-53ef-9f1c-67543d48af1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474658} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9bc8a91-e457-52a8-8f08-fda3fc0e439f" :answer-field/key "$R$ is reflexive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475255} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9273fd00-18f4-5b63-bc77-9c6f1bb11883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474660} {:answer/id #uuid "c3bd68a0-ec14-5260-8301-38a62f7933fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3bd68a0-ec14-5260-8301-38a62f7933fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474661} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a6b08e0-fb69-544a-8ab3-cb721d261941" :answer-field/key "$R$ is symmetric" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475256} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3662c536-6969-5d0f-8633-2687b51453b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 