reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* reflexive because $(\\gamma ,\\gamma )\\notin R.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive because for all $x,y,z\\in {\\alpha ,\\beta ,\\gamma },$ if $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,z)\\in R,$ then $(x,z)\\in R.$ Recall that it's sufficient to check only the cases when both pairs have different components: \n\n- $(\\alpha ,\\beta )\\in R$ and $(\\beta ,\\alpha )\\in R,$ and also $(\\alpha ,\\alpha )\\in R$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $(\\beta ,\\alpha )\\in R$ and $(\\alpha ,\\beta )\\in R,$ and also $(\\beta ,\\beta )\\in R$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's not reflexive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$R$ is symmetric”; “$R$ is transitive” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b70dd396-b01a-51e6-a52c-8ff729f48c45" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Standard Relation Is an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9c693d2-46aa-5f80-92e0-a0d25e335e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474650} {:answer/id #uuid "9eb32df2-8320-5fa4-96f0-b0f567cf3c41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9c693d2-46aa-5f80-92e0-a0d25e335e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.