olution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(a,a),\\,(b,b),\\,(c,c)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is symmetric because $(y,x)\\in R$ whenever $(x,y)\\in R.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* transitive because $(a,b)\\in R$ and $(b,c)\\in R,$ but $(a,c)\\notin R$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's not transitive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$R$ is reflexive”; “$R$ is symmetric” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56e1a8e8-e6fa-5d18-a8ea-e9b55d53facb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474644} {:answer/id #uuid "a170fea6-c960-5d28-8f6b-a9fccc84dc24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56e1a8e8-e6fa-5d18-a8ea-e9b55d53facb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474644} :answer-field/id #uuid "37822b3d-3a59-510a-95d2-92a92f197a69" :answer-field/key "$x\\,R\\,y$ if ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475248} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff715192-cc17-5c8e-a4f8-34655ead00e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474646} {:answer/id #uuid "a9bd81fd-3f13-5e06-83a1-1858bec49e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9bd81fd-3f13-5e06-83a1-1858bec49e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474647} :answer-field/id #uuid "0090e86d-3a63-5637-95dd-754c6bdd62bf" :answer-field/key "$x=y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475249} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cef306a2-a1d6-50c7-8fae-5fc70f54757a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474648} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f71df1-4716-5108-9e03-cef2e2d0d244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cef306a2-a1d6-50c7-8fae-5fc70f54757a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474648} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6d6c947-e684-53b2-8702-320415a16119" :answer-field/key "$x\\,R\\,y$ if $xy\\in N$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78aa39d2-6d95-5a7b-bd86-1b4658d3d903" :question/math-academy-id "q-214247" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are equivalence relations on $Q?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- Relation “$x\\,R\\,y$ if ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4$” is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because ${2}^{2}+{2}^{2}≰4.$\n\n- Relation $x=y$ is an equivalence relation since it's reflexive, symmetric, and transitive.\n\n- Relation “$x\\,R\\,y$ if $xy\\in N$” is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive because $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\notin N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=y$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7f9502e-19c3-58bb-98da-1562e0b0dfd0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90b7f96d-2c26-51b8-a503-b732dd7105e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474638} {:answer/id #uuid "58fade47-8b11-5fab-b25b-851ce73bce58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58fade47-8b11-5fab-b25b-851ce73bce58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474639} :answer-field/id #uuid "4680e212-67d2-5252-a922-ef475a60beba" :answer-field/key "$a\\,R\\,b$ if $a-b$ is a multiple of $2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b7d6869-692f-5caa-9e55-9630f69a0c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474640} {:answer/id #uuid "39b3b2e0-da86-5014-bd8a-ee945f0ebf31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b7d6869-692f-5caa-9e55-9630f69a0c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474640} :answer-field/id #uuid "1378d38d-6558-5839-92ba-4bd5499dd871" :answer-field/key "$a∣b$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475246} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b0ed5c9-e5e6-562a-8122-0bb3e30b37ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474642} {:answer/id #uuid "b94689af-dc54-597e-8c18-94f6e4db05f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b0ed5c9-e5e6-562a-8122-0bb3e30b37ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474642} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b62643e-bd65-5cdf-a6f5-99efc18252aa" :answer-field/key "$a\\,R\\,b$ if $3∣(a+b)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3f6ced1-e3e7-51b2-bdb3-c0561413aee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-214246" :question/problem "Which of the following relations are equivalence relations on $N?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's consider each of the given relations.\n\n- Relation “$a\\,R\\,b$ if $a-b$ is a multiple of $2$” is an equivalence relation. \n\n- It is reflexive because for all $a\\in N,$ we have that $a-a=0$ is a multiple of $2.$\n\n- It is symmetric because for all $a,b\\in N,$ if $a-b$ is a multiple of $2,$ then $b-a$ is also a multiple of $2.$\n\n- It is transitive because for all $a,b,c\\in N,$ if $a-b$ is a multiple of $2$ and $b-c$ is a multiple of $2,$ then\n\n$$\na-c=(a-b)+(b-c)\n$$\n\nis also a multiple of $2.$\n\n- Relation $a∣b$ is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not symmetric since $3∣6$ but $6∤3.$\n\n- Relation “$a\\,R\\,b$ if $3∣(a+b)$” is not an equivalence relation. For example, it is not reflexive since $3∤(1+1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$a\\,R\\,b$ if $a-b$ is a multiple of $2$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "968df6ec-e87e-5770-9c11-e7c8d8a27e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Relations on Finite Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a285ab-48a9-5413-b7da-f2791d21aec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453766} {:answer/id #uuid "818ef40a-7f9f-549f-a73c-ef61315430d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "818ef40a-7f9f-549f-a73c-ef61315430d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/v