pe {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453772} {:answer/id #uuid "a52a0aaf-fd45-5ddc-b8ad-8881a84032fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74744e0f-74ff-5c50-920e-156d87bec376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453772} :answer-field/id #uuid "d347c014-5719-570c-9116-b736f2cfb1f8" :answer-field/key "$R$ is an equivalence relation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae54ed26-0094-5420-99d1-1b8455c5d0e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-214280" :question/problem "Consider the relation $R$ on the set $A={\\alpha ,\\beta }$ defined as \n\n$$\nR={(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),(\\alpha ,\\beta ),(\\beta ,\\beta )}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given a relation $R$ on a set $A$:\n\n- $R$ is reflexive if and only if for all $x\\in A,$ $x\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is symmetric if and only if for all $x,y\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y,$ then $y\\,R\\,x.$\n\n- $R$ is transitive if and only if for all $x,y,z\\in A,$ if $x\\,R\\,y$ and $y\\,R\\,z,$ then $x\\,R\\,z.$\n\nIf $R$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive, then $R$ is an equivalence relation.\n\nLet's consider each of the properties in turn.\n\n- The relation $R$ is reflexive because $(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),(\\beta ,\\beta )\\in R.$$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The relation $R$ is *not* symmetric because $(\\alpha ,\\beta )\\in R$ but $(\\beta ,\\alpha )\\notin R.$\n\n- The relation $R$ is transitive because it contains no \"linked\" pairs such that $(x,y)\\in R$ and $(y,z)\\in R.\\,✓$\n\n- The relation is *not* an equivalence relation since it's not symmetric.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$R$ is reflexive”; “$R$ is transitive” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421484 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3888085d-918f-58a3-8bd9-367a97d32018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474562} {:answer/id #uuid "3e335ed9-b0c7-50b7-bf4b-dc3aedd3cf2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3888085d-918f-58a3-8bd9-367a97d32018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474562} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e29da06-bfce-529c-931f-97c2357fe6fc" :answer-field/key "$(x,y,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad121aa6-d319-5297-af2a-e5e3093bb81a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474564} {:answer/id #uuid "c0be6723-f4cc-55bc-99d0-0ee75e7b4417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0be6723-f4cc-55bc-99d0-0ee75e7b4417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474565} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b29ca3-f143-548a-ae89-a64c0ea33837" :answer-field/key "$((x,x),1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd45a65d-0d13-5724-926d-fad0cc9c4e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474566} {:answer/id #uuid "822c7061-50fc-56dd-a5fd-3acb6e1d930d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "822c7061-50fc-56dd-a5fd-3acb6e1d930d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474567} :answer-field/id #uuid "ace444cf-7548-524c-92d8-dd3be4616e9d" :answer-field/key "$((y,x),2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd7d0702-ab54-5763-af3c-93c657eacc9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181974" :question/problem "If $A=\\{1,2,3\\}$ and $B=\\{x,y\\},$ which of the following elements belong to $(B\\times B)\\times A?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $B\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${x,y}$ with ${x,y},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/5a/5af389ab817ce509519af7a3c1a5fdbb583d8e13859b9aa3b6166958f81e3040.png)\n\nHence, the set $B\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nB\\times B={(x,x),(x,y),(y,x),(y,y)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|B\\times B|=|B|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\n(B\\times B)\\times A\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $B\\times B$ and $A,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/da/dae7febad357be8d9f000c9dc7abfbe97fda34e3e9ff0b0e8ab0289e3c4e782a.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|(B\\times B)\\times A|=|B\\times B|\\cdot |A|=4\\cdot 3=12.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $((x,x),1)$ and $((y,x),2)$ are in $(B\\times B)\\times A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $((x,x),1)$; $((y,x),2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3601ac83-0800-567a-9a0d-4d5c37cef413" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to an Equivalence Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8fb2458-5f62-526c-a4ef-234eebfd2a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474870} {:answer/id #uuid "dedf894e-8578-5838-bb97-a01a04d5b043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8fb2458-5f62-526c-a4ef-234eebfd2a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474870} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5e50a82-11c9-5ec6-83f0-10556f882d83" :answer-field/key "The number $-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475361} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f08c149-5209-5a09-b35d-403519f5bb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474872} {:answer/id #uuid "2bdc995a-9e19-5d0b-8013-21abcf455610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f08c149-5209-5a09-b35d-403519f5bb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474872} :answer-field/id #uuid "817fe686-a8a8-5d25-a62f-e53303899546" :answer-field/key "The number $2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee2df81f-2ec6-525a-a134-5bba469a3318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474874} {:answer/id #uuid "d585ca0c-899d-5058-8710-6692be7979a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d585ca0c-899d-5058-8710-6692be7979a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474875} :answer-field/id #uuid "d662e169-3539-5ca6-8143-0749449a329b" :answer-field/key "The number $8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "071418af-96d7-52c9-8845-42c31b88cc12" :question/math-academy-id "q-77200" :question/problem "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $R,$ defined by $x∼y$ if ${x}^{3}={y}^{3}.$ Which of the following are in the equivalence class $[8]?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The equivalence class $[8]$ consists of the elements that are equivalent to $8$ under the given equivalence relation. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[8] & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,x∼8} \\\\  & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,{x}^{3}={8}^{3}} \\\\  & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,x=8} \\\\  & ={8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $8$ is in $[8],$ while $-2$ and $2$ are not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The number $8$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3601ac83-0800-567a-9a0d-4d5c37cef413" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to an Equivalence Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ffea43b-d86a-56b6-bcdb-ce67bcdc018f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474702} {:answer/id #uuid "d2529ebd-b8d8-5045-af24-d984f85479f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2529ebd-b8d8-5045-af24-d984f85479f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474703} :answer-field/id #uuid "45da432d-dfec-5baf-8401-8d2846f1d77c" :answer-field/key "The number $12$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e71abca-c9a3-5770-8721-0722ffcda4d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474704} {:answer/id #uuid "d573ebbe-f7e5-5ea5-8330-54a24a3ef9bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e71abca-c9a3-5770-8721-0722ffcda4d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474704} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e233bb6-7ce4-57bc-a294-bd1bb72c0ce4" :answer-field/key "The number $-4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e537730-288f-53d7-b55a-154f5a93b6c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474706} {:answer/id #uuid "aa9c5b95-859e-5b11-a4e5-1ab13ca0ba4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa9c5b95-859e-5b11-a4e5-1ab13ca0ba4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474707} :answer-field/id #uuid "b97d107f-11ec-588d-8c72-df0e99d81ee5" :answer-field/key "The number $-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "22db406c-85ef-5a5a-ab22-d062645b4362" :question/math-academy-id "q-221718" :question/problem "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $Z,$ defined by $x∼y$ if $7\\,|\\,(x-y).$ Which of the following are in the equivalence class $[5]?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The equivalence class $[5]$ consists of the elements that are equivalent to $5$ under the given equivalence relation. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[5] & ={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x∼5} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,:\\,7\\,|\\,(x-5)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x=5+7k,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,-9,-2,5,12,19,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $12$ and $-2$ are in $[5],$ while $-4$ is not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The number $12$”; “The number $-2$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3601ac83-0800-567a-9a0d-4d5c37cef413" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to an Equivalence Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22e7b59c-00d2-51c6-999a-36e8f035e54a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474876} {:answer/id #uuid "94a4b4c3-a5b5-5d59-ad59-8d61401ea0b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer