ply." :question/worked-solution "We have $3\\in [x]$ if $3∼x.$ Using the definition of the given equivalence relation, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\cdot 3 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\pi  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x \\\\ -1 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $3\\notin [0]$ because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 0)=1\\ne -1\\,\\times $\n\n- $3\\in [1]$ because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)=-1\\,✓$\n\n- $3\\notin [2]$ because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 2)=1\\ne -1\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $[1]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dacfbca6-6135-5d51-a07e-627fce79dfd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalence Classes Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27afc98a-a963-5726-801e-f24814932ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474708} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9b592b-a126-5e98-882f-fa6560baf569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd9b592b-a126-5e98-882f-fa6560baf569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474709} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d217d7f-285a-533a-b5ba-bb0556c98fb1" :answer-field/key "$[5]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475280} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9064f9c1-0e96-5e2c-827d-3231f222b2d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 1